cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Healed or Hidden? Coding Agents Mask Bugs When Told to Fix Failing End-to-End Tests"
abstract: >-
  Data and code for the paper "Healed or Hidden? Coding Agents Mask Bugs When Told to
  Fix Failing End-to-End Tests": one record per session of a coding agent asked to fix a
  failing Playwright test, the analysis outputs behind the paper's numbers, the prompts,
  the scenarios and the code that ran the study. The data are under CC BY 4.0; the
  README gives the license of each part.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zeng
    given-names: Jie
    affiliation: Carnegie Mellon University
repository-code: "https://github.com/if212/healed-or-hidden"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - end-to-end testing
  - test repair
  - Playwright
